	<font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><b>ShowEQ EFF Contributions</b> <font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"  color="#666686"> (08-19-2002 until 09-19-2004)</font>
	<hr>
	After many sleepless nights and pondering...
<br />

<br />
I've decided to take the plunge and accept responsibility for an <a href="http://www.eff.org">EFF</a> fund sponsored by the ShowEQ community.
<br />

<br />
This is your chance to "give back" to ShowEQ, while also helping a worthwhile cause, namely the <A href="http://www.eff.org">EFF</A>... you know, those folks that protect your right to use program like ShowEQ...
<br />

<br />
If you would like to contribute to the ShowEQ project, you can do so via PayPal.  You can click on the penguin 
<form action="https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr" method="post">
<input type="hidden" name="cmd" value="_xclick">
<input type="hidden" name="business" value="ratt@users.sourceforge.net">
<input type="hidden" name="item_name" value="SEQ EFF Donation">
<input type="image" src="http://seq.sf.net/images/contrib_peng.jpg" border="0" name="submit" alt="Donate to the SEQ EFF Project!">
</form>

Or use this link <A HREF="https://www.paypal.com/xclick/business=ratt%40users.sourceforge.net&item_name=SEQ+EFF+Donation">here</a>!
<br />

<br />
If you do not currently have a PayPal account, and you sign up for PayPal, be sure to put ratt@users.sourceforge.net in the referall box, as it will add an extra FREE $5 to your contribution.  Or you can just click on <a href="https://www.paypal.com/affil/pal=ratt%40users.sourceforge.net">this link</a>.
<br />

<br />
All proceeds contributed to the SEQ EFF Fund will be donated to the EFF on a regular basis (usually when there's enough money in the account to donate).  A portion of the donations will be used to renew the vBulletin license for our message base (approximately $80 as of this writing) on a yearly basis.
<br />

<br />
All verified donators will recieve a tag on the message board indicating they are an "Contributing Member" ... to recieve your tag, you must send the EFF donation  and be sure to include your message board user name in the note.  If you do not wish to be credtied (IE - to remain an anonymous donor) please note that as well.
<br />

<br />
I can't stress enough how important the EFF is to your online freedoms.  It is one of the last bastions of legal sanity in an increasingly insane litigious society.  Any support we can provide to them will be helpful, no matter how small.
	</font>
